# Written by open-lyric's `npm run copy-packages`.
#
# Everything under dist/ is build output, copied here byte for byte. Git must
# not touch it: with `core.autocrlf=true` a commit normalises CRLF to LF *in
# the blob* while the working tree still checks out as CRLF, so the mangling is
# invisible here and lands on every consumer — npm installs a git dependency
# from the blob, not from a checkout.
#
# That is not hypothetical. open-lyric-plugin-player@0.1.3 shipped a
# WebAudioFont script 807 bytes shorter than the one its sha384 pin was taken
# from, so every consumer's browser refused it and no chord could sound.
dist/** -text
